# Customer app. Keys without a VITE_ prefix never reach the browser bundle.
#
# Two parts:
#   LOCAL       what the dev server needs: its /api proxy needs both keys (vite.config.ts) and stops
#               with an error without them. Your frontend/customer/.env is this part: copy it.
#               Builds (Vercel, lint) need no .env.
#   PRODUCTION  dummy values (<...> = the real one) for Vercel (Production and Preview) and your private
#               .env.production, which nothing reads (vercel.json takes both keys from Vercel's env).

# ═══ LOCAL (your .env) ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The origin secret /api sends: the public laptop value the local gateway accepts
# (GATEWAY__ORIGIN_SECRETS in backend/bundle/.env.example)
ORIGIN_SECRET=not-a-secret-not-a-secret-not-a-secret
# Where /api goes: the local gateway (npm run dev:backend). The laptop cannot use the live one: the live
# gateway answers only the apps' Vercel hosts. This key also reaches the browser (vite.config.ts): the
# wake-up screen calls its /wake straight, as a sleeping Render service wakes only for a direct call.
BQ_GATEWAY_URL=http://localhost:8080

# ═══ PRODUCTION (Vercel; dummy values) ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ORIGIN_SECRET=<the-same-secret-as-GATEWAY__ORIGIN_SECRETS-in-Render>   (Vercel: Sensitive; vercel.json
#                                                                          sends it as x-origin-secret)
# BQ_GATEWAY_URL=https://bq-live.onrender.com                             (no trailing slash)
